-- No condition reads `amount` or `urgent`, but the condition calls a rule
-- that mentions 50, so the report tries `amount` at 0, 50, 49 and 51, as it
-- tries `days`, and `urgent` at TRUE and FALSE: an input that no condition
-- reads takes the same values as any other input of its kind.
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is late` days IF days GREATER THAN 50

GIVEN days IS A NUMBER, amount IS A NUMBER, urgent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `refund` days amount urgent IS
    IF `is late` days
    THEN amount
    ELSE 0
